WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:07.588
Bobby frowned as he went into the kitchen.

2
00:00:07.589 --> 00:00:10.225
He didn't like cooking class so far.

3
00:00:10.226 --> 00:00:13.896
Chef was strict, and he had so many rules.

4
00:00:13.897 --> 00:00:17.438
But Bobby's eyes lit up when he saw the recipe.

5
00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:20.620
"We're making meatballs!"

6
00:00:20.621 --> 00:00:22.933
"That's right," Chef said.

7
00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:26.216
"Nina and Jason, you can start on the meat mixture.

8
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:29.860
Bobby and Izzie, you can prep the other ingredients."

9
00:00:29.861 --> 00:00:35.179
"I wanted to do the meat," Bobby mumbled.

10
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.210
Izzie started chopping a garlic clove.

11
00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:42.866
Chef gave Bobby an onion. "You can chop this."

12
00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:45.974
"That sounds fun," Bobby thought.

13
00:00:45.975 --> 00:00:52.331
He quickly got started.

14
00:00:52.332 --> 00:00:56.031
"Bobby!" Chef frowned.

15
00:00:56.032 --> 00:00:59.062
"There are rules for using knives.

16
00:00:59.063 --> 00:01:02.040
Keep the point of the knife on the cutting board.

17
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:05.445
Then move the knife up and down—like this.

18
00:01:05.446 --> 00:01:09.105
The onion needs to be finely chopped."

19
00:01:09.106 --> 00:01:14.317
"Yes, Chef." Bobby didn't know what was wrong with his way.

20
00:01:14.318 --> 00:01:17.083
And the onion was making his eyes water.

21
00:01:17.084 --> 00:01:19.476
He wiped his eyes.

22
00:01:19.477 --> 00:01:24.701
"Now your hands aren't clean, Bobby!" Izzie said.

23
00:01:24.702 --> 00:01:29.120
"Clean hands are a kitchen rule," Chef said.

24
00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:31.516
"Go wash your hands again."

25
00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:38.100
Bobby sighed as he walked to the sink. "More rules."

26
00:01:38.101 --> 00:01:41.575
Soon Bobby and Izzie finished chopping.

27
00:01:41.576 --> 00:01:44.768
Chef was standing by the bowl of meat.

28
00:01:44.769 --> 00:01:47.987
"Bring those ingredients over here," he said.

29
00:01:47.988 --> 00:01:53.797
"We already added the egg, bread crumbs, and soy sauce," Jason said.

30
00:01:53.798 --> 00:02:00.025
"Here's the garlic, onion, oregano, and parsley," Izzie said.

31
00:02:00.026 --> 00:02:03.077
She dumped everything into the bowl.

32
00:02:03.078 --> 00:02:05.884
Jason and Nina wet their hands.

33
00:02:05.885 --> 00:02:08.322
Then they mixed everything together.

34
00:02:08.323 --> 00:02:12.548
Chef wet his hands too and grabbed some of the meat mixture.

35
00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:14.917
"Now we'll make the meatballs.

36
00:02:14.918 --> 00:02:19.010
Roll it in your hands until you have a small ball."

37
00:02:19.011 --> 00:02:21.722
Everyone started forming meatballs.

38
00:02:21.723 --> 00:02:24.483
Bobby proudly held up his meatball.

39
00:02:24.484 --> 00:02:28.420
"Look! Mine is almost as big as a baseball!"

40
00:02:28.421 --> 00:02:31.466
"That's too big!" Chef snapped.

41
00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:34.077
"It will take too long to cook.

42
00:02:34.078 --> 00:02:37.084
They should be a little smaller than a golf ball."

43
00:02:37.085 --> 00:02:42.318
Bobby sighed and did as he was told.

44
00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:47.511
The kids put their meatballs on an oiled baking sheet.

45
00:02:47.512 --> 00:02:50.825
"We have to wash our hands again," Jason said.

46
00:02:50.826 --> 00:02:53.270
"We just handled raw meat."

47
00:02:53.271 --> 00:02:57.253
"That's right," Chef said.

48
00:02:57.254 --> 00:03:02.253
He put the meatballs in the oven.

49
00:03:02.254 --> 00:03:05.525
"While they cook, please pick some green beans in the garden.

50
00:03:05.526 --> 00:03:08.659
Another class will cook them tomorrow."

51
00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:12.769
The kids grabbed baskets and went outside.

52
00:03:12.770 --> 00:03:16.783
"It's nice to be outside," Bobby said.

53
00:03:16.784 --> 00:03:20.118
"Chef has too many rules in the kitchen."

54
00:03:20.119 --> 00:03:23.546
"You like sports," Nina said.

55
00:03:23.547 --> 00:03:26.758
"Sports have lots of rules."

56
00:03:26.759 --> 00:03:30.841
Izzie nodded. "They make games fair."

57
00:03:30.842 --> 00:03:35.077
"In the kitchen, rules make cooking safe," Jason said.

58
00:03:35.078 --> 00:03:38.591
"I guess." Bobby shrugged.

59
00:03:38.592 --> 00:03:43.080
When the kids went back inside, the timer was going off.

60
00:03:43.081 --> 00:03:46.456
Chef set the baking sheet on the counter.

61
00:03:46.457 --> 00:03:48.742
"I made a dipping sauce.

62
00:03:48.743 --> 00:03:53.870
It has honey, olive oil, mustard, vinegar, dill, and salt."

63
00:03:53.871 --> 00:03:57.703
"Yum!" Bobby got a meatball and took a bite.

64
00:03:57.704 --> 00:04:01.500
"Ouch! Hot, hot, hot!" he cried.

65
00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.854
"Bobby!" Chef said.

66
00:04:03.855 --> 00:04:07.066
"Never eat anything right out of the oven.

67
00:04:07.067 --> 00:04:09.445
Always let it cool first."

68
00:04:09.446 --> 00:04:12.206
He gave Bobby a cool glass of water.

69
00:04:12.207 --> 00:04:15.569
Bobby swished the water around his mouth.

70
00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:22.971
"I get it now. Kitchen rules are important!"

